{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/innoroutercore\/rejection-reasons"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.core\/documentation\/InnoRouterCore\/Rejection-Reasons"},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"One-stop reference for every rejection \/ cancellation \/ failure","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"taxonomy in the InnoRouter stack — when each case fires, where it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"originates, and how to handle it.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"InnoRouter deliberately surfaces failure modes as typed values rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than opaque codes. Each authority owns its own rejection taxonomy, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"all of them reach consumers through either a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Configuration"},{"type":"text","text":" callback,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the unified "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events: AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":", or a store method’s return value."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In 5.0 that synchronous configuration surface is one typed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onEvent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"callback per store rather than one callback per event case."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The table below groups every rejection type by authority. Follow the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"link under “Symbol” for the full symbol reference with cases and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"associated values."}]},{"anchor":"Navigation","text":"Navigation","type":"heading","lev